# Cursor Rules for web-api

## Critical Directives
- DO NOT run `git commit` or `git push` without explicit user confirmation.
- Always run `go vet ./...` and `go test -count=1 ./...` after modifying Go code.
- Follow Orchid Starter Clean Architecture conventions (refer to AGENTS.md).

## Technology Stack
- Language: Go 1.24+
- Web Framework: github.com/go-chi/chi/v5
- Logger: github.com/olympus-forge/logos
- Errors: github.com/olympus-forge/bunker
- Token / Auth: Dual-Secret JWT + Refresh Token Rotation (RTR)
- CSRF Protection: Double Submit Cookie with HMAC-SHA256 signature
- Cookie: HttpOnly SameSite=Strict/Lax abstractions in pkg/cookie

## Code Structure
- Entrypoint: cmd/api/main.go
- Dependency Injection: internal/bootstrap/container
- HTTP Server: internal/bootstrap/server/restful_server
- Modularity: modules/<module_name>/{delivery,usecase,repository,domain}
- No HTTP imports inside usecase or domain packages.
